Weavers' Row~
   A narrow street of weavers' shops south of the market. The looms are
still working: grey-skinned women sit at them weaving shrouds from thread
spun out of their own hair, and the finished shrouds are stacked to the
ceilings, waiting for a city's worth of dead.
